<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kirn</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kirn is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahe">Nahe River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, at the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunsruck">Hunsrück</a> hills. Above it stands the ruined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyrburg">Kyrburg</a> castle, a seat of the Wild- and Rhinegraves and of their successors, the Princes of Salm-Kyrburg, who ruled the town until the French occupation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> in the 1790s. It later became known for leather-making and brewing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kirn.jpg" alt="Kirn" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagar66 based on work of TUBS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kirn_in_KH.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
